<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neapolitan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Austro-Neapolitan War · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neapolitan War was fought in 1815 between the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joachim-murat">Joachim Murat</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>. During <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a>, Murat declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and called for Italian unity, but he was defeated at Tolentino in May 1815. Murat fled, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> king Ferdinand IV was restored to Naples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neapolitan-war.jpg" alt="Neapolitan War" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Schirmer, k. u. k. Oberlieutenant, zugetheilt dem Generalstabe, ü. c. im Infanterie-Regimente Philipp Herzo... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_map_of_the_military_operations_of_the_Austro-Neapolitan_War_of_1815.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
